WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.488
In the year 234, the Shu Han army was stationed at Wuzhang Plains, its banners fluttering in the wind.

00:00:07.838 --> 00:00:11.726
This was Zhuge Liang's fifth northern campaign, and everyone was full of hope.

00:00:12.076 --> 00:00:17.428
Zhuge Liang toiled day and night, writing countless military orders, and his body grew weaker and weaker.

00:00:17.778 --> 00:00:21.450
Late into the night, he still sat before the lamp, handling military affairs one by one.

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:27.320
Ill, Zhuge Liang called his generals to his bedside and charged them to continue the northern campaign and complete the great cause.

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:31.750
The generals knelt by the bed, tears in their eyes, and nodded their promise.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:37.380
One night in the eighth month, a great star fell from the sky, streaking across the night.

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:45.122
The Shu Han chancellor Zhuge Liang died of illness in the army, only fifty-four years old, and the whole army grieved beyond measure.

00:00:45.472 --> 00:00:48.880
The soldiers lowered their heads, quietly seeing him off.

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:56.262
His feather fan lay quietly on the desk, as if still guarding the dream of Shu Han.

00:00:56.612 --> 00:01:01.004
People will always remember this loyal and diligent chancellor.

